# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every
# platform and whatever core.autocrlf says. For the shell scripts
# this is not a preference: CRLF in a shebang line
# (#!/bin/sh\r) silently breaks the interpreter, and bin/ and the
# hooks carry no extension a narrower pattern could catch.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Git detects binaries on its own; naming them keeps a stray
# byte from ever tipping one into text handling.
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
